THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

The library depends on Mathlib (https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4),
Copyright (c) the mathlib4 authors, licensed under the Apache License, Version
2.0. Lake fetches it at build time, at the revision recorded in
lake-manifest.json; no Mathlib file is included in this repository.

ToMathlib/ holds general mathematics written for this library. Where a file
there extends a Mathlib file, it has the same relative path and contains only
the additions.


NIELSEN AND CHUANG

The library formalizes results and exercises from Quantum Computation and
Quantum Information by Michael A. Nielsen and Isaac L. Chuang (Cambridge
University Press), each cited by item number and page. The book is not
reproduced: each item is stated in Lean and summarised in a sentence of our
own, and comments quote short phrases of the book only where its wording bears
on how a statement should be read. Rights in the book remain with its rights
holders, and nothing granted above extends to them.
